Box 1-1:  Diagnostic clues for Diarrhoea
yy
Diarrhoea WITH vomiting, low grade fever with no mucus in stools: consid­
er viral infection
yy
Diarrhoea WITH vomiting, fever, abdominal cramps, blood and mucus in 
stools: consider  bacterial infection
yy
Diarrhoea WITH blood and mucus in stool WITHOUT fever: consider amoe­
biasis
yy
Profuse diarrhoea present (rice water stools) WITH vomiting: consider chol­
era
yy
Diarrhoea WITH excessive vomiting (especially if in more than one member 
of the household or group): consider  food poisoning
yy
Diarrhoea presenting with oral and/or skin lesions, weight loss etc. over 
long period: consider HIV
yy
Diarrhoea alternating with constipation in adults: consider bowel malig­
nancy 
