yy
Diminished skin turgor 
yy
Altered consciousness, depending on the degree of dehydration
Investigations
yy
Detection of rotavirus antigen in stool by an enzyme immunoassay 
(EIA)
Treatment 
Treatment objectives
yy
Correction of fluid and electrolyte deficits'),
('3','Constipation','1','Disorders of the Gastrointestinal Tract  ................................','19','19-21','yy Inability to move bowels yy Passing hard stools yy Infrequent passing of stools yy Straining to pass stools yy Feeling of incomplete evacuation of bowel yy Inability to pass flatus, colicky abdominal pain with or without vomiting','yy Frequent high pitched bowel sounds - suspect mechanical bowel obstruction yy Absent bowel sounds - suspect paralytic ileus yy Signs of peritonitis (generalised tenderness, guarding and rebound tenderness, refer appropriate section) -`suspect gangrenous bowel','yy Digital rectal examination (must be carried out in all patients with suspected diagnosis of constipation) yy Stool for occult blood yy Plain abdominal X-ray (erect and supine) yy Proctoscopy/proctosigmoidoscopy/colonoscopy (must not be done if acute intestinal obstruction is suspected)','Treatment objectives yy To identify possible cause of constipation yy To relieve constipation Non-pharmacological treatment yy Adherence to regular exercise yy High fibre diet yy Adequate fluid intake (minimum of 3.2L of water per day if no contraindications exist) — Constipation — Chapter 1: Disorders of the Gastrointestinal Tract 21 Pharmacological treatment A. Management of Constipation in Adults 1st Line Treatment Evidence Rating: [C] yy Bisacodyl, oral, 10-20 mg at night Or yy Senna, oral, 15-30 mg at bedtime (maximum 70-100 mg daily). Doses above 70 mg should be divided 12 hourly Or yy Lactulose, oral, 15-30 ml daily until response, then 10-20 ml daily 2nd Line Treatment Evidence Rating: [C] yy Bisacodyl, rectal, 10 mg in the morning Or yy Glycerol suppositories, rectal, 4 g at night Or yy Liquid paraffin, oral, 10-30 ml at night Or yy Milk of Magnesia, oral, 5-10 ml in a glass of water, 12-24 hourly B. Management of Constipation in Children 1st Line Treatment Evidence Rating: [C] yy Lactulose, oral, 10-18 years; 15 ml 12 hourly 5-10 years; 10 ml 12 hourly 1-5 years; 5 ml 