10.	 Acute Hepatitis
Hepatitis is defined as inflammation of the liver and has multiple 
causes. It may present as an acute illness with jaundice and altered liver 
function tests. When symptoms, signs or laboratory abnormalities persist 
for more than 6 months it is considered chronic.
