Chapter 2: Disorders of the Liver 
41
Referral Criteria 
Refer all cases of chronic hepatitis B infection to a specialist, 
especially those who have failed first-line anti-viral therapy or had 
adverse reactions to anti-viral therapy or have liver-related complications 
(e.g. liver cirrhosis, liver failure, liver mass, signs of portal hypertension, 
ascites, peripheral oedema, hypoalbuminaemia). Pregnant individuals 
and patients with hepatitis B co-infections (e.g. HIV/Hepatitis C) as well 
as those requiring chemotherapy or other immunosuppressive therapy 
should also be referred to a specialist.
