34.	 Sick newborn 
The term newborn (neonate) refers to a baby in the first month of 
life. At birth all healthy newborns are active with a strong cry. Any baby 
born ill will show signs of poor activity or may be described as “being flat” 
or floppy in severe cases. The newborn with one or more abnormal vital 
signs is unwell. These include colour, activity, temperature, respiration, 
heart rate, blood sugar, urine output, nature of bowel movements, signs 
of distress (pain).
