41.	 Chest Pain
Chest pain is a common patient complaint and must be treated as 
a medical emergency until proven otherwise as there are several life-
threatening underlying causes. The top priority is to exclude or promptly 
treat serious cardiac and non-cardiac causes. A good history and 
examination is very helpful in this endeavour. 
